"use strict";
window.LC_CHUNKS=window.LC_CHUNKS||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["university_mathematics_en"]=window.LC_CHUNKS["university_mathematics_en"]||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["university_mathematics_en"][8]={"university_mathematics_en:M8-L1":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L1\">M8-L1 – Homotopy and fundamental group<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M8 – Algebraic topology<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor’s studies · Elective<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_mathematics&amp;module=M2&amp;lesson=L4&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M2-L4<\/a>; <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_mathematics&amp;module=M5&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M5-L3<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>Classification:<\/strong> Bachelor specialisation and bridge\nto master-level studies<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Learning objectives<\/h2>\n<p>You define homotopies of paths with fixed endpoints, construct the\nfundamental group and explain its group structure. You prove that the\ndisk has trivial fundamental group while the circle has fundamental\ngroup isomorphic to the integers. You calculate winding numbers of\npolygonal loops and distinguish topological proof from numerical\nsampling.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Paths and homotopy relative to endpoints<\/h2>\n<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nbe a topological space and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=[0,1]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nA path is a continuous map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><mi>I<\/mi><mo>→<\/mo><mi>X<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha:I\\to X<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nPaths\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>β<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha,\\beta<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwith identical endpoints\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a,b<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nare homotopic relative to their endpoints if there is a continuous map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><mi>I<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>I<\/mi><mo>→<\/mo><mi>X<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H:I\\times I\\to X<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nsuch that<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"1.0em\"><\/mspace><mi>H<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>β<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"1.0em\"><\/mspace><mi>H<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"1.0em\"><\/mspace><mi>H<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H(t,0)=\\alpha(t),\\quad H(t,1)=\\beta(t),\\quad H(0,s)=a,\\quad H(1,s)=b.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>Joint continuity in both variables is essential; an arbitrary family\nof continuous paths is insufficient. A loop at basepoint\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nsatisfies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=b=x_0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe constant loop is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c(t)=x_0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nA loop is nullhomotopic if it is homotopic to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>c<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nrelative to the basepoint. The relation is reflexive via\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H(t,s)=\\alpha(t)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nsymmetric by reversing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>s<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nand transitive by joining two homotopies at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s=1/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe pasting lemma for continuous maps on finitely many closed subsets\nensures continuity at the join.<\/p>\n<p>In a convex subspace of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℝ<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R^n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>+<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mi>β<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H(t,s)=(1-s)\\alpha(t)+s\\beta(t)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis always valid. In a nonconvex space the entire homotopy must stay\nwithin the space; straight-line interpolation can leave it.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Fundamental group and functoriality<\/h2>\n<p>The fundamental group\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>X<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_1(X,x_0)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nconsists of homotopy classes of based loops. For loops\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>β<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha,\\beta<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ndefine<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo>*<\/mo><mi>β<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">{<\/mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mn>0<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><\/mtd><\/mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>β<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>t<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>.<\/mi><\/mtd><\/mtr><\/mtable><\/mrow><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\alpha*\\beta)(t)=\\begin{cases}\\alpha(2t)&amp;0\\le t\\le1/2,\\\\\\beta(2t-1)&amp;1/2\\le t\\le1.\\end{cases}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>The multiplication\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mi>β<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo>*<\/mo><mi>β<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[\\alpha][\\beta]=[\\alpha*\\beta]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis well defined: paste two homotopies in the path variable in the same\nmanner. Associativity holds for classes, not necessarily for\nparametrised paths. The two bracketings traverse the same three paths\nwith different time allocations; continuous linear interpolation between\ntheir monotone piecewise linear reparametrisations gives a homotopy. An\ninserted constant path segment can likewise be removed by\nreparametrisation. Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[c]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis the identity. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mover><mi>α<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾<\/mo><\/mover><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\bar\\alpha(t)=\\alpha(1-t)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe formula\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>t<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H(t,s)=\\alpha((1-s)\\min(2t,2-2t))<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ncontracts\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α<\/mi><mo>*<\/mo><mover><mi>α<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾<\/mo><\/mover><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha*\\bar\\alpha<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nsimilarly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mover><mi>α<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾<\/mo><\/mover><mo>*<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\bar\\alpha*\\alpha<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ncontracts. Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mover><mi>α<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾<\/mo><\/mover><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[\\bar\\alpha]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis inverse to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[\\alpha]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/p>\n<p>A continuous based map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>X<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>→<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>Y<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><msub><mi>y<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:(X,x_0)\\to(Y,y_0)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ninduces the homomorphism\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mo>*<\/mo><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mi>f<\/mi><mo>∘<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_*([\\alpha])=[f\\circ\\alpha]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nsince composition with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\npreserves homotopies and concatenations. For composed maps,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>g<\/mi><mo>∘<\/mo><mi>f<\/mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>*<\/mo><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>g<\/mi><mo>*<\/mo><\/msub><mo>∘<\/mo><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mo>*<\/mo><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(g\\circ f)_*=g_*\\circ f_*<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIn particular a homeomorphism induces an isomorphism. Fundamental groups\nneed not be abelian and are not complete invariants.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Circle, disk and winding number<\/h2>\n<p>Identify the plane with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℂ<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nSet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{<\/mo><mi>z<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>z<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S^1=\\{z:|z|=1\\}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{<\/mo><mi>z<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>z<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D^2=\\{z:|z|\\le1\\}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIn\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>D<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D^2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>+<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H(t,s)=(1-s)\\alpha(t)+s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ncontracts every based loop, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msup><mi>D<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{<\/mo><mi>e<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_1(D^2,1)=\\{e\\}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor the loop traversing the circle once, the same construction does not\nstay in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>S<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S^1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-mathematics-en/media/img/U_MAT_039_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Once-around circle loop, based contraction in the disk and lifts with endpoints −1, 0, 1.\" />\n<figcaption aria-hidden=\"true\">Once-around circle loop, based\ncontraction in the disk and lifts with endpoints −1, 0, 1.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>S<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S^1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nconsider\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>u<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><mi>u<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p(u)=e^{2\\pi i u}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u<\/mi><mo>∈<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℝ<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u\\in\\mathbb R<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nEvery continuous loop\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>α<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha(0)=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nhas a unique continuous lift\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><mi>I<\/mi><mo>→<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℝ<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a:I\\to\\mathbb R<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nsatisfying\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a(0)=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p(a(t))=\\alpha(t)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nTo justify this, use uniform continuity to subdivide\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfinely enough that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>−<\/mo><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>t<\/mi><mi>j<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|\\alpha(t)-\\alpha(t_j)|&lt;1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\non each subinterval. The quotient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mi>α<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>t<\/mi><mi>j<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha(t)/\\alpha(t_j)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthen has a continuous principal angle\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>∈<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mi>π<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>π<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\theta(t)\\in(-\\pi,\\pi)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwhich is zero at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>t<\/mi><mi>j<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_j<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nPut\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>t<\/mi><mi>j<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>+<\/mo><mi>θ<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a(t)=a(t_j)+\\theta(t)/(2\\pi)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthere; successive pasting constructs the lift. Two lifts differ\ncontinuously by integers and agree initially, hence everywhere.<\/p>\n<p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p(a(1))=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe value\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>∈<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℤ<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=a(1)\\in\\mathbb Z<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis the winding number. For a based homotopy\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>H<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nuniform continuity on the square supplies one fine subdivision in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>s<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe same angle construction with quotients\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mi>H<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>t<\/mi><mi>j<\/mi><\/msub><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H(t,s)/H(t_j,s)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nyields a lift\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ncontinuous in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(t,s)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A(0,s)=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIts endpoint\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A(1,s)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis integer-valued and continuous, hence constant. Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis homotopy invariant.<\/p>\n<p>Conversely, any lift ending at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis homotopic relative to endpoints in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℝ<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nto the linear path via\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>+<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1-s)a(t)+snt<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nApplying\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nshows that every loop of winding number\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis homotopic to the standard loop\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^{2\\pi i nt}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nEvery integer occurs; concatenation adds endpoints because the lift of\nthe second path starts at the endpoint of the first. Consequently<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msup><mi>S<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msup><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>≅<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℤ<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>+<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_1(S^1,1)\\cong(\\mathbb Z,+).<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>The circle and disk therefore are not homeomorphic. Nor can a\nretraction\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><msup><mi>D<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>→<\/mo><msup><mi>S<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r:D^2\\to S^1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r<\/mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><msup><mi>S<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msup><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">id<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r|_{S^1}=\\operatorname{id}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nexist: composing a contraction of the once-around loop in the disk with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>r<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwould contract a winding-one loop within the circle. For the punctured\nplane\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℂ<\/mi><mo>\\<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C\\setminus\\{0\\}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>z<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>+<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mi>z<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>z<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(z,s)=((1-s)+s/|z|)z<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis a deformation retraction onto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>S<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S^1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nHence its fundamental group at basepoint 1 is also isomorphic to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℤ<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb Z<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msup><mo>×<\/mo><msup><mi>S<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S^1\\times S^1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe two coordinate winding numbers classify the loops, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msup><mi>S<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msup><mo>×<\/mo><msup><mi>S<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msup><mo>,<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>≅<\/mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℤ<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_1(S^1\\times S^1,(1,1))\\cong\\mathbb Z^2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nHomotopies in both components can be performed together; concatenation\nadds componentwise.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Polygonal winding number and sampling limitations<\/h2>\n<p>For a closed polygonal loop with vertices\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><mo>,<\/mo><mi>…<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><msub><mi>z<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>z<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_0,\\ldots,z_N=z_0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin the punctured plane, suppose every segment avoids the origin. The\nangle change along a straight edge is then the principal angle of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>z<\/mi><mrow><mi>j<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><msub><mi>z<\/mi><mrow><mi>j<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mover><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>z<\/mi><mi>j<\/mi><\/msub><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><msub><mi>z<\/mi><mi>j<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><mo accent=\"true\">¯<\/mo><\/mover><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(z_{j+1}/|z_{j+1}|)\\overline{(z_j/|z_j|)}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mi>π<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>π<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-\\pi,\\pi)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIndeed a segment avoiding the origin lies in an open half-plane bounded\nby a line through the origin (take the normal from the origin to the\nclosest point of the segment, for example). The total winding number is\nthe sum of these angles divided by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\pi<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWith exactly opposite directions the segment passes through zero and the\nmethod is undefined.<\/p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre\nclass=\"sourceCode python\"><code class=\"sourceCode python\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><a href=\"#cb1-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"im\">import<\/span> cmath<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"><a href=\"#cb1-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"im\">from<\/span> math <span class=\"im\">import<\/span> pi, fsum<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-3\"><a href=\"#cb1-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-4\"><a href=\"#cb1-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> polygon_winding(vertices, tol<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"fl\">1e-10<\/span>):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"><a href=\"#cb1-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"co\"># Explicitly closed polygon; all vertices and edges avoid 0.<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-6\"><a href=\"#cb1-6\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">len<\/span>(vertices) <span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">2<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">or<\/span> vertices[<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>] <span class=\"op\">!=<\/span> vertices[<span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>]:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-7\"><a href=\"#cb1-7\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">raise<\/span> <span class=\"pp\">ValueError<\/span>(<span class=\"st\">&quot;closed polygon required&quot;<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-8\"><a href=\"#cb1-8\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">any<\/span>(<span class=\"bu\">abs<\/span>(z) <span class=\"op\">&lt;=<\/span> tol <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> z <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> vertices):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-9\"><a href=\"#cb1-9\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">raise<\/span> <span class=\"pp\">ValueError<\/span>(<span class=\"st\">&quot;vertex too close to zero&quot;<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-10\"><a href=\"#cb1-10\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    angles <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> []<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-11\"><a href=\"#cb1-11\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> a, b <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">zip<\/span>(vertices, vertices[<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>:]):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-12\"><a href=\"#cb1-12\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        q <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> (b<span class=\"op\">/<\/span><span class=\"bu\">abs<\/span>(b)) <span class=\"op\">*<\/span> (a<span class=\"op\">/<\/span><span class=\"bu\">abs<\/span>(a)).conjugate()<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-13\"><a href=\"#cb1-13\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        theta <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> cmath.phase(q)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-14\"><a href=\"#cb1-14\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> pi<span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"bu\">abs<\/span>(theta) <span class=\"op\">&lt;=<\/span> tol:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-15\"><a href=\"#cb1-15\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">raise<\/span> <span class=\"pp\">ValueError<\/span>(<span class=\"st\">&quot;edge through or nearly opposite zero&quot;<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-16\"><a href=\"#cb1-16\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        angles.append(theta)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-17\"><a href=\"#cb1-17\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    turns <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> fsum(angles)<span class=\"op\">/<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>pi)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-18\"><a href=\"#cb1-18\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    n <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">round<\/span>(turns)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-19\"><a href=\"#cb1-19\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">abs<\/span>(turns<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>n) <span class=\"op\">&gt;<\/span> tol:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-20\"><a href=\"#cb1-20\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">raise<\/span> <span class=\"pp\">ArithmeticError<\/span>(<span class=\"st\">&quot;numerically uncertain result&quot;<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-21\"><a href=\"#cb1-21\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> n<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-22\"><a href=\"#cb1-22\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-23\"><a href=\"#cb1-23\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> polygon_winding([<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>, <span class=\"ot\">1j<\/span>, <span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>, <span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"ot\">1j<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>]) <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-24\"><a href=\"#cb1-24\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> polygon_winding([<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>, <span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"ot\">1j<\/span>, <span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>, <span class=\"ot\">1j<\/span>, <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>]) <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><\/span><\/code><\/pre><\/div>\n<p>The code computes the winding number of the polygon, not necessarily\nthat of an unknown smooth path between samples. For instance, sampling\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><mn>8<\/mn><mi>t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^{2\\pi i 8t}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>j<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mn>8<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=j/8<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ntheoretically always yields 1; the interpolated polygon is constant but\nthe true path winds eight times. For a known circle loop whose lifted\nangle change between sample endpoints is strictly less than\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>π<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin magnitude on every interval, the unwrapped increments agree.\nFloating-point tolerances are additional practical checks, not rigorous\ninterval arithmetic; for very small or nearly opposite points, rescale\nor check at higher precision.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-assessment<\/h2>\n<h3 id=\"exercises\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Give a based homotopy of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^{2\\pi it}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nto the constant loop in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>D<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D^2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWhat happens at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=s=1/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Find the winding number of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mi>t<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^{2\\pi i(3t+\\sin(2\\pi t))}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand of the reversed path.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Find the class of the concatenation of standard loops of winding\nnumbers 4 and −7. Why is it not nullhomotopic?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Prove that two based circle loops with equal lifted endpoints are\nhomotopic, without differentiating the curves.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Compute the winding number of the polygon\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>i<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1,i,-1,-i,1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand explain why the edge from 1 to −1 is invalid in the punctured\nplane.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<details class=\"lc-solutions\" data-lc-section=\"S6\"><summary>Show solutions<\/summary>\n<div>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><mo>+<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H(t,s)=(1-s)e^{2\\pi it}+s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=s=1/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nit equals 0, outside\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>S<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S^1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nbut inside\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>D<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D^2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The lift\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mi>t<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a(t)=3t+\\sin(2\\pi t)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nstarts at 0 and ends at 3; the reversed path has winding number −3 (lift\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>−<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a(1-t)-3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>).<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The class corresponds to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>7<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4-7=-3\\ne0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℤ<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb Z<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nA based homotopy cannot change the integer endpoint.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a,b<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nare lifts with initial value 0 and common endpoint\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>p<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>+<\/mo><mi>s<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H(t,s)=p((1-s)a(t)+sb(t))<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis a continuous based homotopy. Differentiability is not required.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Each of the four edges contributes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>π<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\ngiving\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\pi<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand winding number 1. The segment from 1 to −1 contains the origin.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/div>\n<\/details>\n<h2 id=\"S7\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://math.uchicago.edu/~farb/algtop2023/Hatcher.pdf\">Allen\nHatcher – Algebraic Topology<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · §1.1, Theorem 1.7; path homotopy and\nproduct groups · Last accessed: 2026-11-24 · Content verified:\n2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://people.math.wisc.edu/~lmaxim/751f14w3.pdf\">Laurentiu Maxim\n– Math 751, Lecture Notes Week 3<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · §1, Theorem 1 and Lemmas 1.1–1.3\n· Last accessed: 2026-11-24 · Content verified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>"};
